      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "GiveDirectly's operational model is built on low-cost delivery and high transparency. They spend only <cite id=\"11\">$0.05 to raise every $1</cite>, which is significantly better than many humanitarian peers. Their commitment to evidence is reflected in their <cite id=\"12\">98.8 Impact beacon score</cite> from Charity Navigator. Furthermore, the charity has <cite id=\"13\">delivered over $117 million directly to recipients</cite> in a single fiscal year, demonstrating massive scale. This scale is supported by a <cite id=\"14\">board of 9 members</cite> providing rigorous oversight of global operations."
      ],
      "summary": "GiveDirectly is a humanitarian organization that focuses on reducing poverty through <cite id=\"1\">direct cash transfers to individuals</cite> in Africa and the United States. Since its <cite id=\"2\">founding in 2009</cite>, the charity has championed the model of unconditional cash aid, allowing recipients to prioritize their own needs. In FY2024, the organization managed <cite id=\"3\">total revenue of $206,811,067</cite> to support its global relief programs. The charity maintains a <cite id=\"4\">94/100 overall score from Charity Navigator</cite>, reflecting high standards of accountability. Their operations are characterized by high efficiency, with a <cite id=\"5\">program expense ratio of 91.8%</cite> reported in recent filings. This distinction is important for donors seeking to fulfill specific religious obligations. The charity has <cite id=\"7\">delivered cash to over 2 million beneficiaries</cite> across countries like Kenya, Malawi, and Rwanda. By removing intermediaries, GiveDirectly aims to <cite id=\"8\">establish cash as a benchmark</cite> for the social sector. Their model is backed by a <cite id=\"9\">strong theory of change</cite> and verified outcome tracking. This approach provides a transparent way for donors to see exactly how their funds reach those in extreme poverty.",
